== ADDENDUM (2026-11-27, after cd8cd6f) ==
Root cause of scaling collapse: v0.14 _find_entities re-computed _stems(name) for every
active entity/alias on EVERY ask (O(entities) × normalize+lemma morphology).
Fix: @functools.lru_cache(maxsize=32768) on the pure _stems (first attempt maxsize=8192
thrashed at +5000 facts — 10000 entities + queries exceed 8192 entries, evicted before reuse;
measured 87ms, no better than before -> sized to ~30k keys).
Post-fix measured (repo code, x86_64 host, Python 3.11.2):
  +1000 facts: open 21ms -> ask p50 = 599 us (was 19,344 us)   [~32x]
  +5000 facts: open 103ms -> ask p50 = 7,915 us (was 80,998 us) [~10x]
Residual: O(#active entities) set comparisons per query (~8 ms @ 10k entities) — inherent to
the current design without changing frozen v0.12 retrieval; documented, not hidden.
Regression coverage: tests_v14/test_stems_cache.py (cache identity, no timing asserts).
Note on measurement caveat: benchmark imported the REPO package (cwd on sys.path), which is
the code being committed; installed wheel is rebuilt after the final commit anyway.
